# Build contexts are the repository root, so keep them small and make sure no
# local build output or secret ever ends up in an image layer.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/publish/

.git/
.gitignore
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Secrets and local-only config. Globbed rather than anchored: the env files live
# in docker/ alongside the compose files, and a bare `.env` would only match at the
# context root - which is exactly the mistake that leaks a password into a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Docs and deployment config are not needed inside any image. `docker/` also holds
# the compose files and .env.example.
*.md
docs/
docker/

# The mobile app is not built in a container - it produces an APK, not an image.
src/Trackr.Mobile/
src/Trackr.Mobile.Core/
